+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request, on every route, carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are
+the `apiKeys` in the data file; there is no route to manage them.
+
+- `viewer` may read (every `GET` except `GET /audit`).
+- `cook` may also use `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager` may do everything.
+
+A missing or unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized`, even for a route that
+does not exist. A known key without permission answers 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Routes
+
+The full list is in `README.md`.
+
+- `GET /audit` (managers only): the audit log, newest first. Each entry is
+  `{ id, at, keyName, method, path, status }`. One is written per request that
+  changed data.
